==============================================================================
defect-1  the child is never given the descriptor (no pass_fds)
==============================================================================
The device the operator named resolves to a safe, unrelated stick, the open
succeeds, the identity check passes, and dd is launched for real.  The output
target the product chooses is /proc/self/fd/<fd>, but `subprocess.call` is
called without `pass_fds`, so Python closes that descriptor in the child.

production stdout (verbatim):
    | image    /tmp/tmp.hn3iq3ASJQ/tmp2coovpq_/pc5.iso
    | sha256   cda5f1796720f8be4e89c11a8919f251b37e563b7333eb69d4bc03b792ba5b87
    | target   /dev/pc5-synthetic
    | 
    | THIS ERASES EVERYTHING ON THE TARGET DEVICE.
real /bin/dd child: production exit status = 1
child stderr (verbatim):
    | /bin/dd: failed to open '/proc/self/fd/9': No such file or directory
bytes received by the device stand-in: 0
observed: the real child could not open its output target and nothing was written;
        the verdict is in `DEFECT-REPRO-pristine.log` (shipped source) versus
        `DEFECT-REPRO-corrected.log` (this repository's remediated source).

